=== E1. With and without the filter.  All modes keep every answer reachable: within a size level they test first,
and evaluate the rest of the level afterwards unless the answer was found. ===
first   = label-feasible candidates are evaluated and stored first, then the others (class order changes).
lfprobe = label test, then an exact row-by-row test against the target (stop at the first mismatch) on what
          the labels let through; nothing is stored unless it is the answer; then the plain pass in plain order.
probe   = the same with NO labels: the exact row-by-row test on every candidate of the target's type.
audit   = plain search with every candidate label-tested: a FALSE REJECT is a ruled-out candidate equal to the target.
quotients (par mod3 sgn) on integers; sequences unlabelled (AT says 'anything' unless the index is negative); all rows checked.
times: fastest of 3 runs, full GC before each.

